  "verbalization": "Oblonganoside C is implicated in the regulation of Casein kinase I isoform gamma-3 through a multi-step pathway involving Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The evidence suggests that Oblonganoside C acts as a target of Ent-Gloeosteretriol, which in turn modulates the activity of Casein kinase I isoform gamma-3. This relationship is supported by multiple high-scoring paths, with scores ranging from 0.6121 to 0.6484, indicating a consistent and plausible mechanistic link. The core mechanism appears to involve Ent-Gloeosteretriol as a central mediator, where it exerts its effects on Casein kinase I isoform gamma-3 through the inhibition of its activity. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Oblonganoside C in modulating the activity of this kinase, possibly through the regulation of Ent-Gloeosteretriol. The evidence supports a biologically plausible mechanism, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction and its functional implications.",
